!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Unstaged in the tree and NOT a lane's to move: `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`, and the `mempalace` submodule pointer — never commit, stash, or revert those. The `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` pointer reads differently: the operator PINNED it at `4afa852`, the released 3.0.0, and the grammar's own head stands ahead of that pin while its 3.0.1 line runs unmerged. A lane still leaves it alone; the operator moves it, and a `git log` on that gitlink shows their pin rather than drift.
* ''Landed since'' (CHANGELOG, THE HOSTED WALK, THE HOSTED WALK, MADE SOUND and THE HOSTED WALK'S AFTERMATH): the hosted walk (F1), then its cleanup (B1) — the leaf-bound retry; carriage keyed by the proven leaf; the live wallet; host and walk running inside the standing vessel over the one store door; the per-hearth hosting doc; the node's `lares walk` verbs, walking and hosting as the worn face, at one hearth; a charterless herm answering the knock (`ownPlacePosture`); a vessel under `LAR_ROOT` projecting into that root; ROOT-ON-FOUNDER pinned; the pinned docker mesh; the tree-clean witness; the staged `hosted-walk` acceptance — then its aftermath: the hosting modules naming only what stands, `mesh-scenarios` reading a hearth whose latest boot died as not stood, the road to Stable founding in canon, and the adapter note naming `LAR_ROOT` as the isolation knob.
* ''Landed since (round 6 series, `c687ab03d..HEAD`, CHANGELOG):'' leaves of one PersonaGroup sync through a herm with no listening vessel, over a leaf-peer session the proof binds (per-direction keys, a hash chain, divergence surfacing); the persona-KEL fold turns verify-then-fold — only a candidate that verifies competes at each seq, a quorum-signed fork surfaces rather than a silent pick, and the three keyhive doors surface `unreadable`; the herm's drop-door admits only a successor that verifies against its carried predecessor, capped and journaled; a hung herm no longer wedges a leaf's dial; the addressed envelope and the grammar-wasm CI step; the held-out reader's github-context fidelity, genesis and provisioning fixes; `doctype-render-parity` proves off a committed before-render fixture, never off history a squash merge can erase. Measured, not assumed: run `tools/witness-all.sh` and the whole e2e set fresh before trusting a count below this line.
* ''Landed since (golden path P2.5, `07fd0df09..116d1848d`, CHANGELOG):'' eight cuts close NO GLOBAL NOW: verdicts and causal stamps/fences; durable receipt doors; clockless persona admission; CAS retention by verified fence; monotonic local liveness; residency verbs that report state; no-back-compat evergreen sweeps; and supporting instruments. See the eight CHANGELOG groups for behavior and SHAs.
* ''E2E'' (CI shards at `116d1848d`): 31/31 files, 173 tests; `MERGE-VERIFY ok=true`.
* ''Unit suites'' (all under a scratch `LAR_ROOT`, with `LAR_BAGS` unset; measured at `116d1848d`): memetic-frame 357; mesh 2755 (12 skip); keyhive 163 (1 skip); tw5 1765 (6 skip); node 1683 (1 skip); browser 153; lares-cli 658 (5 skip). Supporting suites: mempalace 80; sensorium 52; web 11. All suites read 0 failures.
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): 11 projects clean at `116d1848d`. Import failures: none across the measured suite logs.
* ''Witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`): 35/35 run one at a time and green at `116d1848d`; tree-clean, civic, crossing, herm-mesh, browser-weld, and witness-all remain by-hand/skipped. `git status --porcelain` read identical before and after the run.
* ''HEADS-UP — the operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'': its stored device edges carry signatures over the clocked layout, and any rotated seal lineage it holds carries no signed rolls. Both fail verification on this build. Pin sidecars carrying `expiry`, undotted circle stamps, and lineage-less charters also refuse on this build. A fresh start by hand stays the cure. Do NOT stand that vessel on this build; it needs a fresh start, by hand (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/fresh-start`).
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the operator pushes; `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names the run for the pushed head, and anything committed after it waits for the next push. `held-out.yml` parses again (`00c679e97`) and runs weekly or by hand; no hosted run of it has yet read green.
* ''The docker mesh'' (by hand; `witness-all` runs none of it): `crossing-witness` 4 of 4; `node tools/mesh-pins.mjs --up` stands the mesh pinned; `herm-mesh-witness` carries `node/alpha` across three hops, verified at the last; `mesh-scenarios nexus` reads every step ok, the hearths carrying from the herm. A hearth whose log carries a `[lararium] fatal:` line reads as not stood.
* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail when a browser or server socket stands absent.

