!! Open wounds, ranked

The hosted walk, its cleanup and its aftermath stand, the three B1 rulings enacted (the worn face hosts; a herm answers the knock; a boot follows `LAR_ROOT`). Nothing below blocks a push; the rulings owed read in ''Pending operator rulings''.

''P2.5 residue, ranked'' (episkopos handoff `gp25-ep7.md`; P2.5 closed, these ride the next path):
# ''M13 — writes into a retired bag can strand successful writes in its old doc.'' CREATE after DROP re-points the sole registry row to a fresh doc; a prior COPY still succeeds against the retired doc. Next lane: refuse write verbs by name and point to CREATE; decide DROP's true removal (registry row and recipe slot) and add a single-read retirement marker. Red-first X rows in `probe-k1.sh`.
# ''P2.5 residue, ranked: L19–L25 next; L18 after those.'' L19–L20: REPACK refusal hints and live request-id reporting. L21: `vessel read sensorium` and `recall --limit` fall through. L22: stale captured-epoch wording. L23: source archaeology and stale prose: `action-handler.ts` says LOAD fetch remains unimplemented and names no live CREATE or REPACK handlers; `sense.ts` says retired spellings answer `unknown command` instead of the usage refusal; `persona-admit-flow.ts` still says an offer may have expired; `cabal-vouch.ts` misstates its refusal conditions; `lares.ts` retains reboot-to-switch and `--expires` wording; test titles and comments retain lane labels. Further L23/L24 residue includes comments/readers in `index.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `residency-actions.ts`, `daemon-vm-core.ts`, `nexus-publish.ts`, `ingest-core.ts`, `device-delegation.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `seal-reserve.ts`, `mesh-palace.ts`, `cleanup-days.ts`, `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, and `archive-envelope.ts`. L24: back-compat wording in source comments and tolerant readers. L25: CREATE scans every tiddler to detect retirement. L18: `alreadyStood` still reports `count: 1`. Source corrections remain outside this meme-only change. Full itemization: `gp25-ep7.md` §1 and the YANG audit.
# ''Design residue.'' Outcome-doc rotation; `committed`-then-crash to `interrupted` by boot epoch; production wiring for `KeyhiveIdentitySlot`; herm cancel/receipt routing; full-corpus per-verb flush re-measure; clock-7's pack-PIN recursion and `assertBodyIndexTier` caller.

''Landed in golden path P2'' (through `5dd6bf96c`): plugins load by recipe on all four island paths; genesis holds only the boot set; `nexus publish` reads a local offering source; the parked-request deadline reaches the caller's decision; the after-roll refold gets awaited; and the merge gate checks each file. The fix pass after the GP3 review (`4bb57320f`, `a71f4b57b`, `a63cb9980`, `bb3a909b4`, `75d0886ab`) closes H1′ (a vessel frozen while serving drops a verb whose caller hung up or whose deadline passed), M-a (the wedged holder names its pid by the staging bind name), M-d (publish refuses `boot-set-unknown` without genesis), L-d, L-e and L-f. R1–R4 landed; provenance sits inside the signed preimage; the highlight stands as the PoC, published unsigned and signed by the publishing persona. Streams leaves genesis for a deferred crossroads offering. R5 dissolved into the genesis re-bake.

''Open findings from the GP3 review'' (`gp3-episkopos.md`; the struck ones read above):
# ''M-b — recipe wiring lacks a vessel-level proof.'' No test drives a recipe that names an offering through a vessel path. Three of four path mutations stay green: node daemon VM, browser pool, browser daemon VM; the node-pool spread variant also stays green while a source-shape regex catches only the narrower mutation. Resolver tests prove the selector, not vessel wiring.
# ''M-c — refold answers overclaim.'' `represented:true` survives a swallowed re-presentation error or no dial; `admit-take` folds `"pending"` into false; `after-roll-awaited.test.ts` reads source shape only and cannot observe those outcomes. The live refold path reads true or pending within its budget.
# ''M-e — realm steward key needs a ruling.'' The Docker `meme` scenario fails at “B edits, promotes”: the steward gets named by a per-Nexus LEAF key, while realm-bag co-sign looks for the persona ROOT key. This failure predates P2. Rule which key names a steward on a realm doc, then align the realm verb and harness.
# ''L-a'' — `minted-canon-projection` has a phase-marker race; poll for the wiki slug or live marker.
# ''L-b'' — an unbounded `afterRollChain` stage can stall later rolls and leave refold answers pending indefinitely.
# ''L-c'' — `pokeSealHomeRefold` maps a failed refold to `none`.
# ''L-g'' — `tw5BinPath` records a constant rather than a measured path.
# ''L-h'' — `vessel found` reads `$LAR_ROOT/genesis` and ignores `LAR_GENESIS`.

# ''THE RE-FOUND, one train'' — the rulings that shape it, the slices in dependency order, and the questions the operator still owns read in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`. It mints unversioned names, re-mints the engine and edge, and re-seats the Nexus; DESTROY-class strings stay frozen. The train: R-STORE ‖ R-CUSTODY → R-CHARTER (the one AID train, the Stable founding act inside it) → R-WIRE → R-ENGINE · R-EMBER · R-KAHU.
## ''No pave or wipe command'' (operator-ruled; such a command is too risky). A fresh START runs BY HAND: move the old homes aside — rename, never delete, so it stays reversible — then found fresh. Valuable data lives in git, in the private `claude-backup` repository, or on `D:` (`stable-founding-road#/fresh-start`).
